    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c5c261c_874a83ac",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/tasks.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 1478788
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-21T10:39:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I combined the \"if\"s and added the comment, for structuring this I was thinking about moving the `k_tid_t` pointer to `task_ctx_base_data` so that we can cycle through it in the same way as we do it below here, but then we\u0027d still need special cases and a note to manually map those thread ids, so I\u0027ve figured I may as well go this way to keep the diff minimal in this file.\n\nHard to say if we\u0027ll have more of these, on one side we only have these two \"system\" threads for now, but then we are certainly going to have more non shimmed threads showing up (there\u0027s already one: https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx_common_pwrseq_sm_handler.c;l\u003d479;drc\u003dcc64bd97f25244e7facc3f6bbfb12c7362f9f19c).\n\nI\u0027m thinking long term what we need is a redesign of the task code to use a couple of iterable sections so we can have the details on the specific driver rather than filling tasks.c with quirks. I could work on that on a followup, what do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "a9c33b06_f2a7a16d",
